# CODEOWNERS — issue #799
#
# Why this file exists
# -------------------
# Reviews of pull requests touching the highest-risk parts of this repository
# were previously routed to nobody in particular: the only bindings were the
# reviewer's own judgement. That is fine for `docs/` and less fine for
# `contracts/`, which custodies real payment-token funds once deployed and is
# effectively immutable afterwards, or for the backend's authentication and
# rate-limiting code.
#
# How matching works
# ------------------
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom and the LAST matching pattern wins, so the
# broad catch-all appears first and the specific, highest-risk paths last.
#
# A pattern that ends in `/` matches a directory and everything below it, so
# `/contracts/` covers `contracts/**` (the pattern named in issue #799).
#
# Routing a reviewer is not the same as *requiring* one. GitHub only makes these
# approvals blocking when branch protection enables "Require review from Code
# Owners" — see docs/code-ownership.md for the exact settings and the
# admin steps that turn this file into an enforced control.

